  "headline": "Stew Buys the Name, Stover Buys the Depth",
  "publicationDraft": "Stew bought the reigning Offensive Player of the Year at a discount, but Michael Thomas arrived with more baggage than a holiday flight: ankle and hamstring injuries, six missed games and a disciplinary benching. Stover turned the risk into DJ Moore and Clyde Edwards-Helaire, both immediate starters. The two newcomers combined for 39.50 in Stover’s Week 11 victory over Stew. Thomas returned respectably before landing on injured reserve in December; Moore missed Week 14 on the COVID list, and Edwards-Helaire suffered a late-season injury. Stover even left an officially ruled-out Edwards-Helaire in his Week 16 lineup. The historical snapshots favor Stover’s realized production, contradicting the old archive. Stew's buy-low idea was defensible; the payoff wasn't. Grades withheld pending reconciliation.",
